---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Move Your Contacts and Calendar';
const description =
  'The next chapter after your inbox — moving your contacts and calendar off Google. Still being written. Check back soon.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-20 pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-brand)]">
        Next chapter
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-balance font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-[var(--color-brand-dark)] sm:text-4xl">
        {title}
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This one’s still being written. Moving your contacts and calendar is the natural step
        right after your inbox — and I’d rather take the time to get it right than rush a
        half-baked version out the door.
      </p>

      <p><strong>Stay tuned. It’s the next chapter.</strong></p>

      <p>
        In the meantime, if you haven’t finished the inbox move yet, that’s the place to be:
        <a href="/move-your-inbox">Move Your Inbox</a>. Or head
        <a href="/start-here">back to Start Here</a> for the lay of the land.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
